9, 10; also when in genitive dependent on an anarth. noun (Bl., §46, 6), Mat.27:43, Luk.3:2, Rom.1:17, 1Th.2:13; as pred., Lk 20:38, Jhn.1:1, and when the nature and character rather than the person of God is meant, Act.5:29, Gal.2:6, al. (M, Th., 14); \n __(b) more freq., with art.: Mat.1:23, Mrk.2:7, al. mult.; with prep., ἀπὸ τ. θ., Luk.1:26; ἐκ, Jhn.8:42, al.; παρὰ τοῦ θ., Jhn.8:40; π. τῷ θ., Rom.9:14; ἐν, Col.3:3; ἐπὶ τῷ θ., Luk.1:47; ἐπὶ τὸν θ., Act.15:19; εἰς τ. θ., Act.24:15; πρὸς τ. θ., Jhn.1:2; with genitive of person(s), Mat.22:32, Mrk.12:26, 27, Luk.20:37, Jhn.20:17, al.; ὁ θ. μου, Rom.1:8, Php 1:3, al.; ὁ θ. καὶ πατήρ κ. τ. λ., Rom.15:6, Eph.1:3, Phi 4:20, al.; with genitive of thing(s), Rom.15:5, 13, 33, 2Co.1:3, 1Th.5:23; τὰ τ. θεοῦ, Mat.16:23, Mrk.12:17, 1Co.2:11; τὰ πρὸς τὸν θ., Rom.15:17, Heb.2:17 5:1; τ. θεῷ, as a superl. (LXX, Jos.3:3), Act.7:20, 2Co.10:4; Hebraistically, of judges (Psa.81(82):6), Jhn.10:34\" (LXX), 35.\n (AS)","source_line":2465}],"occurrence_count":1307,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Deus","count":1288},{"gloss":"deuses","count":8},{"gloss":"deus","count":4},{"gloss":"de-Deus","count":3},{"gloss":"DEUS","count":1},{"gloss":"para-Deus","count":1},{"gloss":"nosso","count":1},{"gloss":"Deuscom","count":1}]},"G2389":{"id":"G2389","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2389","disambiguated_id":"G2389 =","unique_id":"G2389","headword":"Ἰαννῆς","transliteration":"Iannēs","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Jannes","definition_en":"Ἰαννῆς, ὁ \n Jannes (cf. Ἰαμβρῆς): 2Ti.3:8.†\n (AS)","source_line":2542}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Janes","count":1}]},"G2474":{"id":"G2474","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2474","disambiguated_id":"G2474 = the Greek of","unique_id":"H3478","headword":"Ἰσραήλ","transliteration":"Israēl","lexical_morphology":"N:N--L","gloss_en":"Israel","definition_en":"Ἰσραήλ (FlJ, Ἰσράηλος, -ου), ὁ indecl. (Heb. יִשְׂרָאֵל, Gen.32:28), \n Israel: ὁ οἶκος Ἰ